<header class="page-hero">
  <h1>skyBlip Go. Add ADS-B with Bravo.</h1>
  <p class="page-hero-subtitle">
    skyBlip Go, Go+, Bravo and Tango are available. The skyBlip Bravo
    firmware is on GitHub, for an X1 you can buy today. The Panel and the skyPost
    stations are in design, on the same code base.
  </p>
</header>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">In the aircraft</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    skyBlip Go receives ADS-L and FLARM. It does not receive ADS-B on
    1090&nbsp;MHz, which airliners, business jets, helicopters and many touring
    aircraft transmit. skyBlip Bravo receives it in the aircraft, with no
    ground station.
  </p>

  <div class="columns">
    <div>
      <h3 id="bravo">skyBlip Bravo.</h3>
      <p>The ADS-B receiver, for your phone or your Go. The hardware, a Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1, is on sale. The skyBlip Bravo firmware is on GitHub.</p>
      <p class="more"><%= link_to_page "skyblip-bravo", label: "skyBlip Bravo" %></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3 id="tango">skyBlip Tango.</h3>
      <p>A Go paired with a Bravo shows ADS-B, ADS-L and FLARM on the Go&rsquo;s radar and broadcasts your position in ADS-L. A Go+ and a Bravo make a Tango+.</p>
      <p class="more"><%= link_to_page "skyblip-tango", label: "skyBlip Tango" %></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">For glass cockpits</p>
      <h3>skyBlip <span class="highlight">Panel</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        A fixed box behind the instrument panel, powered by the aircraft. It will have no
        screen. Traffic will appear on a panel display, such as a Garmin G3X or Dynon
        SkyView, as with factory-installed traffic equipment.
      </p>
      <p>
        It will transmit and receive ADS-L. RS-232 outputs will send FLARM NMEA or GDL90 to the
        electronic flight display (EFIS). It will send GDL90 over Wi-Fi and FLARM NMEA over Bluetooth.
      </p>
      <p class="feature-guide"><small>Hardware: LilyGO T-Beam Supreme, MAX3232 RS-232 adapter.</small></p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot shot--photo">
      <%= pages_image_tag "skyblip-panel-board.avif", alt: "skyBlip Panel: the board in its case, with its antenna" %>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">On the ground</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Around the airfield, a skyPost station will receive ADS-B, add traffic
    from the Open Glider Network (OGN) and weather data (QNH, METAR, TAF), and relay it
    all in ADS-L to every skyBlip Go in range.
  </p>
  <div class="columns">
    <div>
      <h3>skyPost Helio.</h3>
      <p>The solar station. Self-powered, in a weatherproof case on a mast. It will receive ADS-B, ADS-L and FLARM.</p>
      <p class="note">LilyGO T-Beam Supreme, Ebyte E80-900MBL 1090 receiver, LilyGO T-Solar kit.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>skyPost Bridge.</h3>
      <p>For existing stations: OGN, PiAware, adsb.lol. It will relay the traffic they already decode over ADS-L, without changing their data feeds.</p>
      <p class="note">LilyGO T-Beam Supreme.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%= render "shared/cta" %>
</section>
